# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
#
# These used to be Hugo `aliases`, which emit an HTML page carrying a
# meta-refresh. That is slow, it breaks the back button, and crawlers treat it
# as a soft redirect. A 301 here is the real thing.
#
# Reference: https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/

# /docs was never a page. It has always been the guides index under another
# name, and the navigation, footer and 404 all point at /guides/ directly now.
/docs             /guides/        301
/docs/            /guides/        301

# /philosophy-condensed was a near-duplicate of /why-aixgo written at a
# different length. The one section it carried that /why-aixgo did not ("What
# Aixgo is not") was folded in, and the page removed.
/philosophy-condensed   /why-aixgo/   301
/philosophy-condensed/  /why-aixgo/   301
